A||||3||contra||AutoTranny Shift Kits??||||1||
Z||000000||contra||10-03-2000||11:25 PM||||I was wondering if anybody has any auto tranny shift kits installed<P>they're reasonably cheap at only $50 or so, and supposedly make a difference. i was just wondering what kinds of things this will do to my transmission, how hard they are to install, and are they worth the $50?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||80's BOY||10-05-2000||02:12 AM||||well, i bought the one from the fiero store for around 50 bucks or so. is it easy to install? well, it depends on how brave and how good you are with puzzles. if you are an engine builder, it will take about two hours with all the proper tools. did it help? well, harder shifts and higher shift points are better than factory. other than that it's a little disappointing. i'd say it's probably worth it.||||reg||12
Z||000002||theogre||10-05-2000||09:44 AM||||A TH125 in good shape and properly adjusted shift pretty decent I think. The trick is getting the TV cable set just right. It's not quite as self adjusting as the procedure in the books makes it seem.<P>A shift kit won't help a tranny with problems and worse it could mask problems.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||contra||10-05-2000||06:22 PM||||cool<BR>my tranny is perfect<BR>i just want it to shift better<BR>i think i'll look into the shift kit<BR>it'll cost me half a day's work so i dont care<BR>||||reg||1
